            <ArticleTitle>[A supracondylar process in a child with arm pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A9028</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 14-year-old boy had arm pain after a traumatic event. An X-ray showed a supracondylar process of the humerus, which is a coincidental finding but sometimes has clinical consequences. It may compress the median nerve or brachial artery, leading to symptoms. Resection can give complete relieve of symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
